    "author_association": "OWNER",
    "body": "## Summary\n\n- Fixed short keyboard viewport geometry on the existing mobile shell branch.\n- When the keyboard is open and focus is in #dmInput or #reportInput, the existing mobile layout controller scrolls the active field into the visible DM panel.\n- The compact profile bar scrolls horizontally without clipping dynamic name/stat/argument pills; the menu button stays fixed and clickable.\n- The regression runner uses the app's original style.css import cascade. Missing scenarios and runner exceptions fail explicitly; fixture skips are listed separately and excluded from PASS totals.\n\n## Scope\n\nOnly these five paths differ from the PR base:\n\n- `AsyncScene/Web/ui/ui-core.js`\n- `docs/ui/ui-core.js`\n- `AsyncScene/Web/style-base.css`\n- `docs/style-base.css`\n- `tools/test_mobile_shell_regressions.html`\n\nWeb/docs mirrors are byte-identical. PR #453 and other workstreams are untouched.\n\n## Verification on exact HEAD `f5c6e90d04109e674918d1041a3f8593049f627c`\n\n- Headless Chromium, all seven sizes: **168/168 PASS**.\n- Fixture-only checks not represented by available data: **10 SKIP**, explicitly excluded from PASS. These cover game action entry and saved panel scroll position in the five mobile/tablet sizes.\n- `python3 tools/test_mobile_first_interface_contract.py`: **14/14 PASS**.\n- Node syntax checks for both UI-core mirrors and inline regression runner: PASS.\n- Exact GitHub Actions `ai-forensics-evidence` run [40918435603](https://github.com/samuray-games/AsyncScene/actions/runs/40918435603): SUCCESS.\n- Independent exact-head review: `PASS_WITH_LIMITATIONS`. A mutation that moved both DM fields outside the viewport produced the expected regression failure.\n- Physical iPhone/Safari and a native OS keyboard were not tested. Keep this PR Draft for owner review; do not treat this as merge or device acceptance.",
